ume


update the architecture+design+requirements+specification docs for the ume platform, integrating in:

the ume platform deploys distributable+deployable+configurable+release operating systems for organizations+businesses, termed "OrgOS", that have configurable/plug-and-play modules that can be flavored/tailored to a specific organizations needs. The ume platform itself is an operating system that serves as a factory for producing tailored operating systems for any organization/business/business-solution. The ume platform provides the baseline infrastructure+kernel for running "orgAps" organization applications, where these applications manage/run an organization (an organization runtime). "Organization Runtimes" realize "organization outcomes", goals, objectives, milestones, tranformations, and so on... An organization effectiviely becomes a series of interconnected running OrgApps all specified, configured, maintained, managed and defined under an OrgSystem, create SDOs software defined organizations, which act as "digital twins" of a physical organization/business. Users operate and interact with SDOs, at the digital twin layer. OrgExec(utors) and OrgCPUs are the running components that take action and execute OrgSystem commands/tasks, with OrgExecs being humans+AI+agents+hybrid systems+custom physical agents and OrgCPUs being digital-agents+machines+devices+3rd party platforms/tools+IoT devices/sensors+, where common interfaces for OrgCPU/OrgExec to OrgKernel/OrgSystem are defined through ODDs organization device drivers, OrgDeviceDrivers. ODDs orgDeviceDrivers are effectively contracts for how an OrgDevice, an entity which executes work on the system, will carry out tasks on and use the OrgOS, so that other system components+devices can plan accordingly and use these devices as necessary, all through a common, agreed upon operating standard/contract. 

For example, when a new user has an idea and wants to start a new business, they will create an account and bootstrap+configure+design their initial organization+organization-operating-system on the ume platform. The user, any employees/contractors, AI assistants and agents would become OrgExecs, executing tasks for the OrgSystem (the business), where contracts+skills+labor-specification are specified through ODD orgDeviceDrivers. The Ume platform offers a configurable business solution that can scale to any organizatoin size, from single entrepreneur to massive enterprise, while maintaining a common set of standards and best practices. Business+Organizations can be effectively "simulated" through their digital twins (OrgSystems+OrgOSs+OrgKernels) and this allows them to be optimized, better maintained, have single source of ground truths, have master data management (OrgDNA) which can be replicated and transmitted to other orgnaizations, allowing for further optimzation and scaling. 

distributed ledger systems DLTs can exist between/among organizations+organization-operating-systems, where contracts (smart contracts) can be executed on these ledger. DLTs are a representation of OrgMemroy, and the memroy between/among a group of organizations, where resources/data/assets are transfered between/among organizations, as defined and specified by smart contracts between+among organizations. Organizations can connect with one another and scale+compose, forming decentralized autonomous organizations, DAOs, effectively making DAOs a set of interconnected+decentralized+distributed organizaitons, that work in tandem/concert together as one, single organization, facilitating vertical and horizontal organization scaling+growth+composability.

Another example is: say that Bob and Alice want to go into business together as partners and start a dry cleaning business. Ume allows them set up everything they need to get the business up  and running. Ume allows them to configure various business modules, such as an accounting module for setting up bsusiness and tax accounts for the business, a marketing module for configuring compaigns and generating social media tags and post and tagline ideas to generate more awareness and drive customer curiosity, based on micropersonas of their target customer audience, operations module which has a small scale ERP systme for managing and planning out dry cleaning resources such as capital+dryers+washers+coin machines+vending machines and works together with a supply chain and logistics system to help track vendor orders of these resources+cleaning supplies and also helps find and source dry cleaning supplies. The sales and CRM module helps keep track of customer orders, things that customers have to be dry cleaned, helps track how long customer orders are being processed, as in how long it takes for customer orders to be fulfulliled and their items to be cleaned, and returned to a customer from initial drop off. The legal entity module helps generate and keep track of all legal, tax and compliance documentation necessary for making the business legal in any given jurisdiction, as well as provides a database for tax auditors to come in and view if necessary, all easily through a single interface/dashboard. The employee management system helps keep track of and manage employees, track employment applications, works with the legal entity sytsem to keep track of employee contracts+agreements+documents, management employee benefits and tax information. All of the modules of the ume platform can interact, integrate and use applicable and appropriate third party tools to fulfill their functions, such as the sales module using stripe for payments, or the HR/employee system/CRM system using monday for tracking employee data and customer orders. Eventually Bob and Alice would like to set up a franchise of dry cleaning business and also want to start an investment fund for funding that acts as a vehicle for purchasing and rehabing other dry cleaning business, all of these processes which can be handles and coordinated/orchestrated via the ume platform. Alice and Bob form a DAO using ume, in order to handle the autonomous franchisees who want to buy+operate a dry cleaning business from their franchise brand. The dirstributed ledger and smart contracts allow each of the independent+autonomous+decentralied franchisee business owners to indepenedent operate while still aligining with the core brand set forth and maintained by Bob and Alice's parent franchise brandh company. Ume now allows Bob and Alice to scale their business to any size, all through a single, standardized platform.

The entire ume platform ultimately acts as a massive spreadsheet for an entire organiztation, where the spreadsheet is broken into manageable parts and handled by various modules, all orchestrated together via the ume kernel, which handles the core organization spreadsheet. Instead of having a spread sheet with thousands to millions of lines of organization data (organization master data), the ume platform allows users to manage each components/part of the spreadsheet, piece by piece, in a standardized and systematic way, reducing time and complexity of running an organization/business and optimizing on returns and desired outcomes. The ume platform provides the spreadsheet needed to run any organization+businses at any scale, at any time, on demand, simple and straight forward enough to be used by any user.



